well many people walked away with a job  after the mega job fair at the  convention center that happened earlier  on today  yeah this comes as the clock is ticking  on federal unemployment benefits those  are going to expire here in a couple of  months  victoria saha takes a closer look at  what this job fair meant  for people who were out of work the  packed las vegas convention center is a  clear sign that thousands of those who  are still unemployed  are hoping to walk out today with a job  offer and get back  into the workforce kelly andrews is just  one of the thousands that walked into  the job fair not knowing what to expect  but hoped for the best i just got hired  she says she applied to many jobs in the  last several months but  hardly received a follow-up it felt like  on deaf ears until today  and i feel like when you apply online  you're kind of anonymous brandon smith  also shares the same frustration  sometimes i get a call back saying the  position has been filled  sometimes it's usually ghosted i'll say  it's usually ghosted  he didn't get an offer friday but is  expecting a call back  friday's job fair had up to 5 000 job  seekers and roughly 14 thousand  available jobs  with federal unemployment benefits  ending in september  county leaders are glad to see the huge  turnout a lot of people  are still a little bit leery about  getting out in the world so the fact  that  this many people came out is a very  positive sign employers are ready to  hire  at mgm the first hour they gave out 100  job offers  the lines are flooding and we're so  happy to see it  but people are ready to come back to  work and we're ready to put them to work  jobs range from entry level all the way  to corporate level those who didn't land  a job from today's job fair say they  will remain hopeful  and they are glad that they were able to  make that face-to-face connection  reporting from the las vegas convention  center victoria saha 8 news now
 

